# documentation-rule.mdc — Unified Documentation & QRG Standard

_Last updated 2025‑09‑11_

## 1 · Length Budget

**Individual Documentation Rule**: Documentation files should be concise enough to be readily understood. Limit code examples unless absolutely necessary, as the docs will be used by AI but still need to remain human readible.

| Doc Class                          | Target tokens | Hard cap | Action if over cap              |
| ---------------------------------- | ------------- | -------- | ------------------------------- |
| Micro‑guide / README note          | ≤ 1,000       | 1,500    | keep flat file                  |
| Standard spec / ADR                | ≤ 3,000       | 4,000    | split into anchored subsections |
| Complex manual / multi‑topic guide | ≤ 5,000       | 6,000    | enforce hierarchy (§ 3)         |

> **Token** ≈ four characters; use `wc -w` × 1.3 as quick proxy.

## 2 · Hierarchical Structure (Complex Docs)

Documents above **3,000 tokens** **must**:

1. Reside in `docs/<domain>/<topic>/`.
2. Split into child files per major section—named `00-intro.md`,`01-design.md`, ...
3. Include an `_index.md` at folder root acting as the subtree TOC.

## 3 · Quick Reference Guide (QRG)

`_index.md` will be the **top‑level document** in every heirarchy hierarchy and must start with a **QRG block**:

- **Purpose** – one‑sentence summary.
- **Key entrypoints** – list of anchors or child files.
- **Related docs** – sibling or parent links.
- **Master TOC** – link to `docs/README_TOC.md`.

Example:

```markdown
> QRG · Foo Authentication Module
> • Purpose: Sign‑in flow spec & integration notes
> • Entrypoints: [Overview](#001), [API Spec](api-spec.md)
> • Related: [Core architecture](../core-architecture.md)
> • Master TOC: [docs/README_TOC.md](../../README_TOC.md)</topic> </domain
```

## 4 · Master Table of Contents

`docs/README_TOC.md` aggregates all QRG paths; update on every QRG addition/rename.

## 5 · Validation Gate

CI job `docs-lint` fails if any of the following are true:

- Token count exceeds hard caps.
- Complex doc lacks folder hierarchy.
- File or folder missing a QRG block.
- QRG omits link to Master TOC or contains dead links.

---

**Enforcement** — Foreman and BG‑DOC agents must run `docs-lint` locally before marking a documentation task **DONE**.
